@name Diamond triplet 50mm f/2
# Diamond triplet, 50 mm f/2: spherical diamond front element, aspheric
# N-SF11 negative behind the stop, aspheric LuAG rear element (Cooke triplet
# with the stop between elements 1 and 2).
# Why: diamond (n 2.42, V 55) as the positive crown: low Petzval sum and weak
# curves for its power. Material set D (whole catalogue incl. diamond); the
# diamond's surfaces are kept spherical (it is hard to figure).
# Diamond: 24.6 mm across, 4.0 mm thick; single-crystal CVD plates this size are
# not available for optics (see README).
# Bar: 50 mm, 36 x 24, f/2, <= 3 elements, white-light RMS <= ~8 um at 0, 0.7, 1.0
# field, distortion <= 1 %, corner illumination >= 0.35, back focus >= 20 mm.
# Design: lens-render optimize (global search, equal budget for every material
# set): spherical screening of all glass combinations of each topology, then
# aspheric refinement of the best combinations, then 24 starts with one basin
# hop each (this job). Merit: RMS spot at 0, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.85, 1.0 field,
# 440/486/546/656 nm (0.5:1:2:1), object at infinity (1000 m); glass aspheres
# departure <= 0.5 mm. Experiment: lenses/novel/README.md.
# Numbers (lens-render numbers, f/2, infinity): RMS 6.7 / 9.1 / 9.9 um at
# 0 / 0.7 / 1.0 field (flat 440-660 nm: 6.5 / 8.8 / 10.9), distortion +1.00 %,
# corner illumination 0.36, length 61.3 mm, back focus 20.7 mm. At 2.5 m:
# 7.7 / 9.8 / 12.3 um. Misses the 8 um bar at 0.7 and 1.0 field.
#
# Generated by `lens-render optimize lenses/novel/diamond-triplet-f2.toml`.
# RMS spot (4 wavelengths) at f/2, object at 1000 m, by image height
# (fraction of 21.63 mm): 0: 6.6, 0.3: 6.7, 0.5: 8.1, 0.7: 9.3, 0.85: 9.3, 1: 11.6 µm. Units: mm.
#
# Global search: place 1, merit 4.6226e2 (start 20, seed 3).
#
# radius      thickness   material       semi-diameter
  23.2067     4.0153      DIAMOND        12.280
  42.4020     1.9449      air            11.650
  stop        1.3045      air            10.479
  128.7710    6.1200      N-SF11         10.840 k=13.383871 a4=3.529921e-5 a6=-1.290562e-7 a8=3.887076e-10 a10=-7.243083e-13
  21.8293     7.2557      air            7.590 k=2.045274 a4=6.423596e-5 a6=-7.544350e-8 a8=-4.042943e-11 a10=7.463402e-12
  112.3875    19.9285     LUAG           8.580 k=27.335598 a4=7.476085e-6 a6=2.641992e-8 a8=9.855945e-11 a10=7.420153e-14
  -88.5721    38.0000     air            14.270 k=-1.962084 a4=1.754882e-6 a6=-8.505028e-9 a8=-2.497776e-12 a10=1.550565e-13
